        "scope": "Offline static controller4 E802 attr37 auxiliary path; no GPU operations.",
        "findings": {
          "join": "119be0..bf2 constructs GPU+2208 using class D1755E. 11d660..691 loads GPU+88 ChipHal owner; 11d844..868 passes GPU+2208 object and owner as r8 to 1725780, which reads owner+10 word. 17268f8..6959 sets object+179b=1 iff (ChipHal & ~31)==0x20 and low five bits in 5..9; otherwise 0.",
          "families": "Prior pinned 2a9640 native mapping: Ampere native170 impl2/3/4/6/7 -> ordinals2b..2f; Ada native190 impl2/3/4/6/7 ->34..38; Blackwell native1b0 impl2/3/5/6/7 ->41..45; each has +179b=0. Turing native160 impl2/4/6/8/7 ->25..29 and +179b=1. Unknown impl/family not inferred.",
          "effect": "3628a0 returns success before shared auxiliary count+39f4 or other state if object+179b=0. Therefore for the listed GA/AD/GB layouts controller4 attr37 follows same nonauxiliary shared reason0 counter route as media. For Turing auxiliary acquires increment+39f4 and release decrements, with 0/1-boundary firmware 00/16/0a and other state; matching public getter not established.",
          "admission": "GA/AD/GB listed impls may use controller4 with current type3 support, valid reason-mask baseline, paired E802 requests and complete peer reason-mask validation, under the same exact request status and lifetime contract as shipped media. This proves request-mask behavior rather than physical MS residency; current one-device observation not a board allowlist. Turing is not qualified by this audit."
        },
